what REDS %589's booked remainder -- rye/tests/mantra_weave_test.rye still inlines a three-field Line, Diff and Weave and the archive says only that it 'cannot import' the module. Measured on metal this lap rather than asserted, four facts: (1) Zig itself refuses a parent-escaping import, error 'import of file outside module path', so @import("../../mantra/src/weave.rye") from rye/tests is closed by the compiler; (2) a RENAMED symlink beside the test DOES work for a module importing only std -- rye/tests/mantra_weave.rye -> ../../mantra/src/weave.rye compiles and runs Weave.apply and current; (3) it does NOT work for mantra/src/diff.rye, because the rye bridge resolves a symlinked module's own bare-name imports relative to the SYMLINK's directory, so diff.rye asks for weave.rye beside itself and reads FileNotFound; (4) tools/fixtures/r/rye_harness_roster_scan.sh enumerates with -type f -o -type l, so any module placed beside the test reds files_unlisted, gated at zero, and naming the symlink in the harness stem list makes the harness try to rye-run a module with no main. So the port is blocked by the parity corpus admitting no module beside its tests, which is a ruling about that corpus and about rye/ rather than about mantra/. This lap lands only what needs no word: the file's own header, which claims to exercise the pure core of Mantra and to have inlined the model 'from mantra/src/main.rye' -- both false since 20260908.151057, when main.rye began importing weave.rye and stopped declaring Line, Diff and Weave. The header gains the four measured facts and the named doors so the next hand starts from measurement. No module source, no guard, no ceiling, no roster row and no peer file moves; one tracked file.
